{"type":"standard","title":"Katie Hobbs","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Katie Hobbs</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q16226012","titles":{"canonical":"Katie_Hobbs","normalized":"Katie Hobbs","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Katie Hobbs</span></span>"},"pageid":40442614,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Katie_Hobbs_2026.jpg/330px-Katie_Hobbs_2026.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":440},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/02/Katie_Hobbs_2026.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":2037,"height":2714},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1377255258","tid":"9dd42e46-bb4d-11f1-a364-a6b9888efaac","timestamp":"2026-09-28T15:02:26Z","description":"Governor of Arizona since 2023","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katie_Hobbs","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katie_Hobbs?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katie_Hobbs?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Katie_Hobbs"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katie_Hobbs","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Katie_Hobbs","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katie_Hobbs?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Katie_Hobbs"}},"extract":"Kathleen Marie Hobbs is an American politician and social worker serving since 2023 as the 24th governor of Arizona. A member of the Democratic Party, she served from 2019 to 2023 as Arizona's Secretary of State and from 2011 to 2019 as a member of the Arizona Legislature.","extract_html":"<p><b>Kathleen Marie Hobbs</b> is an American politician and social worker serving since 2023 as the 24th governor of Arizona. A member of the Democratic Party, she served from 2019 to 2023 as Arizona's Secretary of State and from 2011 to 2019 as a member of the Arizona Legislature.</p>"}